From: Jan Benedikt <karagos01@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] egl/dri2: fail eglExportDMABUFImageMESA when the fd export fails

dri2_export_dma_buf_image_mesa() ignores the result of the
__DRI_IMAGE_ATTRIB_FD query and returns EGL_TRUE even when the driver
could not export the image, leaving the caller's fds[] untouched. GTK
then builds a dmabuf texture from that garbage value.

This happens with panfrost on panthor, which cannot export a BO that is
private to its VM (the kernel returns -EINVAL from drmPrimeHandleToFD).
GTK's GL renderer exports textures from gsk_renderer_render_texture()
this way, so GNOME Snapshot ends up with a broken GL context and
crashes after a few shutter animations.

Report EGL_BAD_ALLOC instead, closing any fds already exported, so
callers fall back to their non-dmabuf path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Jan Benedikt <karagos01@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c
@@ -2605,10 +2605,26 @@
           *    "If the number of fds is less than the number of planes, then
           *    subsequent fd slots should contain -1."
           */
-         if (i == 0 || is_disjoint)
-            dri2_query_image(image, __DRI_IMAGE_ATTRIB_FD, &fds[i]);
-         else
+         if (i == 0 || is_disjoint) {
+            /* The driver may be unable to export the image, e.g. panfrost
+             * on panthor cannot export a BO private to its VM. Fail instead
+             * of handing back whatever the caller had in fds[i].
+             */
+            if (!dri2_query_image(image, __DRI_IMAGE_ATTRIB_FD, &fds[i])) {
+               fds[i] = -1;
+               if (i)
+                  dri2_destroy_image(image);
+               for (int j = 0; j < i; j++) {
+                  if (fds[j] >= 0)
+                     close(fds[j]);
+                  fds[j] = -1;
+               }
+               mtx_unlock(&dri2_dpy->lock);
+               return _eglError(EGL_BAD_ALLOC, "eglExportDMABUFImageMESA");
+            }
+         } else {
             fds[i] = -1;
+         }
       }
 
       if (strides && !dri2_query_image(image, __DRI_IMAGE_ATTRIB_STRIDE, &strides[i]))
